# Seat 1 declares double riichi waiting on 7m/8m. Seat 0 then closes two
# kans, cancelling ippatsu and exposing three 1m dora and three 5m ura
# (each triplet of indicators points at 222m or 666m, respectively).
# Seat 1 rons 8m with two readings:
# - 222m 333m 444m 666m 88m: Suuankou Tanki, double natural yakuman
#   (26 han nominally, represented as 2 yakuman). Its base is 16000;
#   nondealer ron is 4 * 16000 = 64000. Bonuses do not count.
# - 234m 234m 234m 666m 88m: chinitsu 6 + iipeikou 1 + double riichi 2
#   + tanyao 1 + 9 dora + 9 ura = 28 han. Menzen ron 30 + simple triplet 4
#   + tanki 2 = 36 -> 40 fu. Kazoe is capped at base 8000, so ron
#   would pay 32000. The double yakuman pays twice as much.
# Tenhou treats Suuankou Tanki as single yakuman: both readings pay
# 32000 there, with the natural yakuman winning the tie. Seat 1 pays
# and collects its own 1000-point deposit in either ruleset.

[meta]
name: ambiguous_wait_yakuman_beats_higher_han
title: Double natural yakuman pays more than a 28 han interpretation
rules: both
source: rules.md §3, §4.3, §4.6, §4.33

